From b4125fe6a6d7b109146994cf94ee2967ac80d718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Costa <bruno.costa@cat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:48:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] honda: backport GEARBOX_CVT layout for radarless Bosch
 (audit2 D-1)

Replace the BO_ 401 GEARBOX signals in honda_civic_ex_2022_can.dbc with the
upstream _gearbox_common.dbc GEARBOX_CVT layout (upstream opendbc 9ef0b1fb),
which is what the Honda City 7G was merged against upstream:

  GEAR_SHIFTER 44|5@0+ in byte 5, VAL_ 1 P 2 R 3 N 4 D 7 L 10 S
  (was 5|6@0+ in byte 0 with VAL_ 32 L 16 S 8 D 4 N 2 R 1 P)

Both layouts decode D identically (6116/6116 frames of the City route), but
diverge for S and L. Message name stays GEARBOX, so carstate.py is unchanged.
Affects HONDA_CITY_7G, HONDA_HRV_3G and HONDA_CIVIC_2022 exactly as upstream.

Also normalise pyproject.toml back to LF (5f439d78 was committed with CRLF
by a Windows clone; only the ruff pin remains as a real change).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
